		(property "Notes" "JLC-placed (rev A5; was DNP/hand-fit). 15 A for 100 W out at the 12 V low end (~10 A continuous, 75 % derating). Interrupt 300 A at 24 Vdc (pack max 16.8 V). 3.9 mOhm: 0.4 W at 10 A, give it copper. Review 2 D3: 15 A holds only if the gauge cut-off under load stays at 2.8 V/cell or higher (9.8 A at 100 W); a lower cut-off needs 1206FA-20A"
